module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.ArtinGeometricAxioms
public import WeilConjectures.RingTheory.GRing
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.OpenImmersion
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineScheme
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Pullbacks
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.AtPrime.Basic

/-! # Smooth affine neighbourhoods from Artin's deformation axioms

Source: Stacks Project, Artin's Axioms, Tag 07XY (lemma-get-smooth), with principal
 affine refinement (blueprint: lem-sfb-artin-smooth-point-neighbourhood).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v w

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ArtinGeometry

/-- Every finite-type field-valued object has a smooth representable affine finite-type
neighbourhood. The family is encoded by its functor `a : h_U → F`; its object is the
value of `a` at the identity of `U`. The arrow `b` is the specified fibre isomorphism,
encoded cartesianly over the residue-field point. The equation for `α` specifies the
chosen residue-field isomorphism; because `α` is an R-map, this is an R-isomorphism.
No étale stack descent or surjectivity of this one chart is assumed.
Source: Stacks Project, Artin's Axioms, Tag 07XY (lemma-get-smooth)
(blueprint: lem-sfb-artin-smooth-point-neighbourhood).

Proof:
1. By lem-sfb-artin-rs-versal-formal-object, the Rim--Schlessinger and finite-tangent
hypotheses give a complete Noetherian local R-algebra with residue field K and a versal
formal system whose special fibre is x₀. The G-ring condition includes Noetherianity.
2. FormalObjectsEffective makes this system effective. Localization at the image prime
preserves Noetherianity: every ideal of the localization is generated by its contraction.
It preserves the G-ring condition since its prime localizations are prime localizations
of R. Object descent follows from IsLimitPreserving. Thus
lem-sfb-artin-effective-versal-algebraization gives a finite-type scheme V, a versal
family y, and a finite-type point v with the prescribed residue field and fibre object.
3. OpennessOfVersality gives an open W containing v on whose finite-type points y is
versal. Take a principal affine open U containing v and contained in W.
By lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-section-vanishing-prime it is Spec(B_f). Generators for B/R,
together with f⁻¹, generate B_f/R. The residue field and fibre identification persist.
Finite type of a point is invariant under open restriction: adjoining an inverse of a
nonvanishing g changes generators from K=A_g[c] to K=A[c,g⁻¹], and conversely.
An Artinian local test scheme has one point, so its maps with closed image in U factor
through U. Thus versality restricts with every prescribed identification intact.
4. For every T and object z over T, the diagonal makes
Isom over U ×_S T between the two pulled-back families an algebraic space. Its projection
to T presents h_U ×_F h_T, proving IsRepresentableByAlgebraicSpaces a.
5. Apply lem-sfb-artin-versal-field-lifting to U and its family. Rim--Schlessinger and
versality at all finite-type points give lifting for all finite-type R-fields, including
finite extensions of the residue field, retaining the prescribed isomorphisms.
6. Apply lem-sfb-artin-representable-infinitesimal-smoothness: U is finite type, F is
limit preserving, the map is representable, and step 5 supplies the lifting property.
Its conclusion is smoothness on every étale scheme chart of every space base change.
The point and fibre identification from step 3 give all remaining clauses. -/
theorem exists_smooth_affine_neighbourhood
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (hR : IsGRing R)
    (F : BasedCategory.{v, w} (Over (Spec (.of R))))
    (hFibred : IsFibredInGroupoids F)
    (hDiagonal : HasAlgebraicSpaceDiagonal F)
    (hLimits : IsLimitPreserving F)
    (hRS : RimSchlessinger F)
    (hInfinitesimal : FiniteInfinitesimalSpaces F)
    (hEffective : FormalObjectsEffective F)
    (hVersal : OpennessOfVersality F)
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [Algebra R K] (hK : Algebra.FiniteType R K)
    (x₀ : Object F (affine R K)) :
    ∃ (U : Over (Spec (.of R)))
      (a : BasedFunctor (discreteModuli (yoneda.obj U)) F) (u₀ : U.left)
      (e : U.left.residueField u₀ ≃+* K) (α : affine R K ⟶ U),
      IsAffine U.left ∧ LocallyOfFiniteType U.hom ∧ QuasiCompact U.hom ∧
      LocallyOfFiniteType (U.left.fromSpecResidueField u₀) ∧
      QuasiCompact (U.left.fromSpecResidueField u₀) ∧
      α.left = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom e.toRingHom) ≫ U.left.fromSpecResidueField u₀ ∧
      (∃ b : x₀.val ⟶ a.toFunctor.obj (CostructuredArrow.mk (𝟙 (yoneda.obj U))),
        F.p.IsHomLift α b) ∧
      IsRepresentableByAlgebraicSpaces a ∧
      ∀ (T : Over (Spec (.of R))) (t : BasedFunctor (discreteModuli (yoneda.obj T)) F),
        ∃ (Z : AlgebraicSpace (Spec (.of R))) (p : Z.obj.obj ⟶ yoneda.obj T),
          HasSpaceBaseChange a T t Z p ∧ CategoryTheory.SpaceMapIsSmooth Z T p := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.ArtinGeometry
